      "created_at": "2018-01-18T22:40:12Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-01-18T22:40:54Z",
      "body": "If I'm understanding the requirements correctly, I think there's two separate ideas combined here.\r\n* The first relates to enabling iframes to send their events so that they can be tracked as part of an amp-analytics configuration. As far as I know, this isn't supported today. It's somewhat related to the idea of the [video interface](https://github.com/ampproject/amphtml/blob/master/src/video-interface.js) supporting analytics, but asked for in a much more generic way, not specific to video. Would be interesting to get @choumx's feedback relating to 2-way messaging here.\r\n* The second idea is related to disallowing tracking when the user has not yet consented to it. It is not reasonable to expect the iframed page to present the consent UI. Therefore, the AMP page needs to handle this by either blocking the iframe or informing it that it cannot perform its own tracking within.\r\n\r\nDoes this sound like an accurate summary?",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
